# Development Flow — TradeFlow BD

## Stack
- Frontend: Quasar 2 SPA (Vue 3 + TypeScript) in `web/`
- Backend: Supabase (Postgres, Auth, Storage, RPCs) in `supabase/`
- Auth: Google OAuth via Supabase; scoped login (`platform` | `app` | `shop`)
- Deploy: Cloudflare Pages (`web/` root, `npm run build`, output `dist/spa`)
- Python ETL: `python/` scripts (PC/WTS product sync) — env shared via `web/.env`
- Types: generated at `web/src/types/database.types.ts` via `npm run backend:types` (re-export: `web/src/types/supabase.ts`)

## App surfaces
- `platform` — superadmin (`/auth/platform/login` → `/platform/dashboard`)
- `app` — tenant admin/staff/viewer (`/:slug/app/*`)
- `shop` — customer storefront (`/:slug/shop/*` or `public_domain` hostname resolve)
- `investor` — read-only investor portal (`/:slug/investor/*`)

## Architecture constraints
- Module pattern: follow the folder you edit — Pinia `page → store → service → repository`, or Vue Query composables + repository. See `docs/architecture/state.md`.
- DB writes: prefer Supabase RPCs over direct client mutations when RLS depends on computed access
- New tables: migration → indexes → RLS → helper functions (`security definer` if cross-table) → RPCs → regenerate types
- Permissions: `authStore.effectiveGrants` + `createAccessGuard`; server via `has_module_action()` / `membership_has_module_action()`
- Data contract order: DB schema → UI data shapes → API/RPC contracts (backend fulfills UI, not vice versa)
- Domain change: `docs/README.md` → module `01-prd.md` → `web/src/modules/<module>/`. New docs: `docs/STRUCTURE.md`. Missing fact: `DOC_GAP`.

## File structure
- `web/src/modules/<module>/` — pages, components, stores, services, repositories, routes
- `web/src/components/` — cross-module shared UI (`ui/` subfolder for primitives)
- `supabase/schemas/` — current SQL ([doc/supabase-schema.md](../../doc/supabase-schema.md)); `supabase/migrations/` — history
- `docs/README.md` + `docs/STRUCTURE.md` — index and how to add docs. Specs: `docs/features/<module>/01-prd.md`. `doc/fix/` — dated fix notes.

## Naming conventions
- Vue SFCs: PascalCase (`TenantPage.vue`)
- Stores: `<module>Store.ts` (Pinia)
- Repositories/services: `<entity>Repository.ts`, `<entity>Service.ts`
- SQL: snake_case identifiers; migration prefix `YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_description.sql`
- RPCs: verb_noun_for_scope pattern (e.g. `list_tenants_for_superadmin`)
- Routes: scope-prefixed (`/:tenantSlug/app/...`, `/platform/...`)

## Patterns & libraries
- Feedback: `web/src/utils/appFeedback.ts` (`showSuccessNotification`, `showErrorNotification`, `requestConfirmation`)
- Images: `SmartImage.vue`, Cloudinary uploader dialog
- Loading bar: `GlobalAjaxBar.vue`
- Shell: `WorkspaceShell.vue` with theme classes (`theme-platform`, `theme-app`, `theme-shop`)
- Treasury pages: `TreasuryPageShell`, `TreasuryStatGrid`, `TreasuryTableWrap`
- Batch costing: `useShipmentItemsCostingCache` / `listShipmentItemsBatch` — never `listShipmentItems` in loops
- List pagination: pass `skip_count: true` on large search/list queries
- Performance: no `backdrop-filter` on static surfaces; opaque surfaces preferred

## Business rules (locked)
- Multi-tenant parent/child hierarchy; stock owned by parent, child display via allocations
- Shop sells from `global_stock_allocations` only (stock-backed shops)
- Four login scopes unchanged; grants from bootstrap `effectiveGrants` + `permissionVersion`
- Sales models: BW, pre-order, K-beauty (`koba`), thrift — `docs/architecture/business-models.md`. Do not mix `global_stocks` with `koba_*` or `thrift_*`.
- Investor portal v1 is read-only (no withdrawal request flow)
- Commerce legacy modules retire toward `shop_order`

## Scope guard for agents
- Tasks touching >3 files or >150 lines: narrow scope per `docs/STRUCTURE.md`
- Do not copy Thrift composable architecture into web — keep module/repository/store pattern
- New docs must follow `docs/STRUCTURE.md` (thin, as-built, no duplicate topics)
- Regenerate types after every schema migration (`pnpm run backend:types:local` on local DB; `backend:types` after remote push)
- Deploy backend: `pnpm run deploy:backend` (push migrations + types)
- **Apply migrations locally (default):** `pnpm run backend:local` — keeps prod snapshot data. See `.cursor/rules/supabase-local-backend.mdc`
- **Empty-DB replay (ordering fix / user asks):** `pnpm run backend:reset` — wipes data; then `backend:pull-prod-data` once if prod rows needed

## Do NOT touch without explicit request
- Generated `web/src/types/database.types.ts` / `web/src/types/supabase.ts` (edit via migrations + `backend:types`)
- Legacy cutover migrations until tenant cutover (`20260709000600_b7_cleanup.sql` chain)
